<h3>Setting up a React project with Create React App</h3>
<p>To set up a React project, use the following command:</p>
<pre><code class="language-bash">npx create-react-app my-app</code></pre>
<p>After setup, navigate to the project directory and start the development server:</p>
<pre><code class="language-bash">cd my-app
npm start</code></pre>

<h3>Understanding React Development Environment</h3>
<ul>
    <li><b>Node.js</b>: Required to run React applications</li>
    <li><b>npm/yarn</b>: Package managers for installing dependencies</li>
    <li><b>React Developer Tools</b>: Browser extension for debugging React applications</li>
    <li><b>ES6+</b>: Modern JavaScript features extensively used in React</li>
</ul>

<h3>JSX - JavaScript XML</h3>
<p>JSX allows writing HTML-like syntax within JavaScript, making React components more readable and maintainable.</p>
<pre><code class="language-jsx">const element = &lt;h1&gt;Hello, React!&lt;/h1&gt;;</code></pre>
<p>JSX gets compiled to JavaScript using Babel before being rendered in the browser.</p>
